{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfcTFQHPaXdL9NSeeNPWP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's a regex for an ISO 8601 calendar date (`YYYY-MM-DD`):\n\n```\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```\n\n- `\\d{4}` matches the four-digit year.\n- `(0[1-9]|1[0-2])` matches the month, 01\u201312.\n- `(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])` matches the day, 01\u201331.\n\nIt matches `2026-10-01`.\n\nIt checks the format and the ranges, but not whether the day exists in that month. `2026-02-31` would still match. Calendar validity (leap years, 30-day months) is best handled by parsing the date in code.\n\nTo find dates inside longer text, drop the anchors and use word boundaries instead:\n\n```\n\\b\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])\\b\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7626, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16975, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7626}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "069089d3-9847-4c88-96f6-cc6414e96d6a", "uuid": "4243704a-1f57-4ec4-82f9-8f71b7e39c24", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T00:20:28.057Z", "request_id": "req_011CfcTFPyo7mHi3La5YAidW"}
